 "display_name": "Ricefield Bamboo Valley",
 "description": "A 300 by 160 foot farming valley: three bands of flooded rice paddies cross the whole width, each costing double movement, broken by raised dirt dikes every ten feet that cost ordinary movement -- several parallel lanes, not one crossing. Bamboo groves at the valley's north and south edges are dense stands that block sight (and cost double movement to push through). A village square of four wattle huts sits at the valley's centre, blocking sight and movement with open doorways; low garden walls give +2 AC cover near its corners. Both sides start at their own end of the valley, screened from the far end by their own tree line.",
